    "reasoning": "All supplied worked answers agree with the mathematics except for two source issues. q-71071: continuity gives (16-12)^2=16. q-149955: the real domain is [0,1], so the limit at negative infinity is undefined. q-128433, q-128483, and q-128475: the scalar triple products are 26, -10, and -22, giving volumes 26, 10, and 22. q-73735 and q-128454: coplanarity requires -3t-6=0 and 6(1-t)=0, respectively. q-73064: f'(u)=9u^2+9>0, so the inverse derivative formula applies globally. q-110046: h tends to positive infinity at both ends of the real line and is not injective; no global inverse exists without a domain restriction. MA's option 1 is the correct formal formula for a chosen inverse branch wherever h' is nonzero, but the question omits that necessary restriction. q-160788: componentwise substitution gives (1,1,0). q-127913: the cross product is (-2,-9,-1), giving triangle area sqrt(86)/2. q-20027: the altitude is sqrt(8)/sqrt(3)=2sqrt(6)/3. q-89660: 4^x+x^2 is strictly positive, so x>=3/2. q-21035: f''=6/x^3 never vanishes; x=0 is outside the domain and is not an inflection point. q-31213: the plotted second derivative changes sign at 0 and 4, but only touches zero at -4. q-4772: s''(t)=2 cm/s^2. The available option 3 has the correct centimeter unit, whereas the worked solution incorrectly states 2 m/s^2. No submitted-grade evidence was supplied; the MA evidence below comes solely from each question's own worked solution.",
